# RETIRED — do not install this as a systemd unit.
#
# A direct `codex app-server` service creates a topology that is incompatible
# with the managed daemon used by `agentctl session mira`, `agentctl attach
# mira`, and codex-umwelt-wake. It may leave the autonomous wake watcher on a
# dead or different socket from the human TUI.
#
# For a supervised Codex boot trial, use the existing generic
# agent-session@mira.service chain instead. It first creates tmux session
# `agent-mira`; the in-pane `agentctl session mira --as-self` invocation then:
#   1. idempotently ensures `codex app-server daemon start`;
#   2. verifies `codex app-server daemon version` and its socket; and
#   3. execs `codex --remote unix://<socket>` in that same pane.
#
# The operator interaction surface is therefore always:
#   agentctl attach mira
#   agentctl attach mira -r   # read-only
#
# A failed/stale socket is intentionally fatal and must be repaired; never
# replace it with a local direct Codex process. This .example remains only as
# a guard against reinstalling the retired direct-app-server architecture.
